bmit them for owner selection, and use subcontractors within 50 miles unless the owner approves a greater distance."},{"brick":"provision","id":"R5","owner":"human_required","text":"Manage the renovation under construction-manager-at-risk terms, commence construction after the GMP amendment or owner notice to proceed, and administer authorized written changes affecting scope, price, or time."},{"brick":"report","id":"R6","owner":"blocked_private_input","text":"Prepare the construction schedule after the GMP amendment and provide monthly written progress updates showing percentage completion and other owner-required information."},{"brick":"monitor","id":"R7","owner":"blocked_private_input","text":"Maintain cost controls against the schedule of values, monitor actual and remaining costs and proposed changes, and report variances monthly to the owner and architect."},{"brick":"validate","id":"R8","owner":"human_required","text":"Comply with applicable laws, codes, public-authority orders, equal-employment requirements, and other required governmental programs."},{"brick":"provision","id":"R9","owner":"human_required","text":"Purchase and maintain the owner-required construction-contract insurance throughout all project phases."},{"brick":"plan","id":"R10","owner":"human_required","text":"If the owner directly purchases kitchen or brewery equipment, coordinate its installation with the supplying vendor."}],"source_url":"https://incouragecf.org/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/Incourage-Construction-Manager-RFP.pdf","summary":"Historical 2015 RFP for construction management at risk of the major renovation of the approximately 20,000-square-foot Tribune Building in Wisconsin Rapids. The engagement combines preconstruction and construction under an AIA A133-based contract and an agreed guaranteed maximum price.","title":"Tribune Building Project - Construction Management Services"}
