ry, original-preserving redaction/versioning, Bates numbering, OCR and batch document generation; victim/witness separation, diversion/specialty-court tracking, configurable file numbering, private notes, flexible case searches and reduced duplicate entry."},{"brick":"monitor","id":"R7","owner":"human_required","text":"Track contract expirations and renewals with calendar/task reminders and customizable contract reporting."},{"brick":"provision","id":"R8","owner":"human_required","text":"Track claims with financial reporting and transfer claim files to litigation when lawsuits are filed."},{"brick":"report","id":"R9","owner":"blocked_private_input","text":"Generate criminal, civil, claims and customized reports, including MNCIS financial updates for restitution/fines, pending cases and VOCA PMT victim-grant reporting."},{"brick":"reconcile","id":"R10","owner":"blocked_private_input","text":"Link email to files and synchronize tasks, calendars and MNCIS court dates with Outlook."},{"brick":"provision","id":"R11","owner":"human_required","text":"Support mobile/remote and requested offline editing (connectivity requirements unresolved), multiple browser sessions, configurable required fields, validation, restricted fields, duplicate alerts/merging and single-editor record locking."},{"brick":"report","id":"R12","owner":"human_required","text":"Provide initial role-specific training, documentation, regular software updates, a formal upgrade/issue process and business-hours technical support."}],"source_url":"https://duluthmn.gov/media/10293/20-09aa-rfp-for-case-management-software-final.pdf","summary":"Historical 2020 RFP to replace the City Attorney\u2019s case-management system with software, necessary hardware, implementation, training and support for approximately 20 named users. Scope spans criminal and civil cases, documents, contracts, claims, reporting, integrations and migration.","title":"City Attorney\u2019s Office Case Management Software Solution"}
