PUBLIC BRIEF: {"buyer":"Clean Power Alliance of Southern California","exclusions":["Private staffing plans, financial constraints, property proposals, due-diligence evidence, and negotiating authority were not supplied; final advice and commitments require the licensed broker and CPA approvals.","Relocation management and tenant-improvement design, architecture or construction-management services are optional under separately negotiated agreements, not automatic baseline work.","A qualifying shared boardroom or tenant improvement may meet the boardroom requirement; LEED certification is preferred, not mandatory. No non-commission fee is assumed.","Experimental boundary: no buyer contact, bid submission, spending, private-system access, or autonomous delivery of the engagement."],"id":"clean-power-alliance-real-estate-brokerage-2019","requirements":[{"brick":"review","id":"R1","owner":"blocked_private_input","text":"Confirm requirements from staffing and space records: downtown Los Angeles or environs, proximity to existing or planned Metro rail, parking, a boardroom of at least 1,500 square feet, compliant and secured-server space at occupancy, and suitable low-voltage infrastructure; require Energy Star labeling within one year, with LEED preferred."},{"brick":"draft","id":"R2","owner":"agent_draft","text":"Draft building-owner and developer solicitation materials stating location, floor-area and floorplate needs, operational requirements, completion schedule, and financial requirements."},{"brick":"retrieve","id":"R3","owner":"human_required","text":"Conduct pre-proposal conferences and answer inquiries, market the opportunity, initially assess responses and building compliance, and arrange site tours for CPA staff and design consultants."},{"brick":"score","id":"R4","owner":"human_required","text":"Evaluate proposals and perform due diligence, establish lease and move-in improvement costs, and recommend a shortlist of facilities."},{"brick":"reconcile","id":"R5",